  "record": "T2 interview, round 1\nT2-A1: 1 (Kernels and the composite (E1, E2), then motion (E3))\nT2-A2: 2 (Raster bytes, plus the composite through each host's painter)\nT2-A3: 1 (Keep them as drafts and revise them after the interview)\nT2-B1: 1 (The brief's set)\nT2-B2: 1 (Part-local logical units)\nT2-B3: 1 (A ceremonial flag on a surface, set by the application)\nT2-B4: 2 (Leave it until stage L or T4 needs it)\nT2-C1: 1 (An engine presentational property driven by transitions)\nT2-C2: 1 (Yes, by the built-in rules once transitions exist (E7))\nT2-D1: 1 (Motion values the control owns, on one clock per window)\nT2-D2: 1 (§9.5 governs)\nT2-D3: 1 (Exponential approach)\nT2-D4: 1 (Every transition jumps to its end and nothing is scheduled)\nT2-D5: 1 (Allow it as a capability only)\nT2-E1: 1 (Move it to an engine primitive with a first-party blur (E9))\nT2-E2: 1 (The engine draws content colour exactly as given)\nT2-F1: 1 (At most 512 declared operations per device pixel, and 4 million per frame for an animated part)\nT2-F2: 1 (At most 8 MB per window, evicting the least recently painted parts first)\nT2-G1: 3 (Rescale quantization to the field's actual tone range)\nT2-G2: 1 (Keep the formula as the approved studies drew it)\nT2-G3: 3 (Draw dithered parts at the nearest integer scale)\nT2-G4: 1 (No hover change) — note: when a mouse isnt hovering over, the button goes away- the bulge flattens. \nT2-H1: 1 (Admit an image role)\nT2-H2: 1 (A grip primitive that fills its part's box with the dot pattern)\nT2-H3: 1 (The control's stable ID, the declared part, and the item's stable ID)\nT2-Z1: 1 (Accept E1 to E11 as the T2 plan)"
